    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426-a2">

                <pb facs="0617" n="493" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg493"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Subenclosure—Translation]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chinese Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">W. W. Ten</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Dean of
                        the Diplomatic Corps</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Pastor</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-12-02"><hi rendition="#italic">December 2,
                        1920</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Monsieur le Doyen</hi>: The Chinese Government
                    frequently makes an appropriation of the surplus funds of the Maritime Customs
                    and from each appropriation 13.7% has been deducted by the Inspector General for
                    the use of the Military Government of the South-West. Now the Military
                    Government of the South-West has already been dissolved, as announced by
                    Presidential Mandate promulgated on the 30th day of the 10th month. Consequently
                    whenever the Chinese Government makes further appropriations of surplus Customs
                    Revenue the whole amount should be handed over to the Ministry of Finance and
                    the practice of deducting 13.7% should be cancelled forever. The Ministry of
                    Finance is instructing the Inspector General <pb facs="0618" n="494"
                        xml:id="pg494"/> to act accordingly and it is my duty to address this Note
                    for the information of Your Excellency and to request you to bring the same to
                    the notice of the Ministers of the Powers interested.</p>
                <closer>[No signature indicated.]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
